nanbeige43 P35: shard shapes for a multi-tile decode batch.

Width-sharded decode tensors become (32, 2*width) above one row tile, the
concatenated-heads/WO intermediate uses block sharding, and the LM-head output
falls back to interleaved L1 because the packaged constant fixes a 32-row shard.
Batch <= 32 is byte-identical (helpers return the packaged values).
Revert if the experiment fails; P32-P35 hold the evidence.

